&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce yourself on Slack and meet your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get oriented in the warehouse, walk through our most-used pipelines with the rest of the team, and read enough of the codebase to start asking useful questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Within your first month, you&#39;ll:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get fluent enough in our Airflow setup and Redshift conventions to navigate the codebase independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope your first real project with a mentor, including the design decisions and trade-offs involved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship your first commit.&amp;nbsp; It could be a bug fix, a documentation update, or a small improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;By the end of your internship, you&#39;ll:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have shipped a pipeline, tool, or infrastructure improvement that the team relies on after you&#39;re gone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have presented your work to the broader team, and walked away with a real sense of what production data engineering looks like day to day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have met with various business owners across the company to build your network and get a feel for how a data team fits into a fast-paced startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
